Q: How do I disable the Drag Fill/ Auto Fill on an IRange object for Spreadsheet Gear .NET? A: <p>My current approach is to create my own CommandManager class, override the Execute function, and implement an Executing event. In my editor, where the WorkbookView is, I subscribe to this event and check if the command display text is &quot;Auto Fill,&quot; then cancel the event.</p>
<pre><code>private void CommandManager_CommandExecuting(object sender, CommandExecutingEventArgs e)
{
    if (Readonly)
    {
        CommandRange cr = e?.Command as CommandRange;
        if (cr != null)
        {
            if (cr.Range?.Worksheet?.Name == Worksheet?.Name)
            {
                if (cr.DisplayText == &quot;Auto Fill&quot;)
                    e.Cancel = true;
                return;
            }
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>public class MyCommandManager : CommandManager { }
</code></pre>
<pre><code> public class CommandExecutingEventArgs : EventArgs
    {
        public SpreadsheetGear.Commands.Command Command { get; }
        public bool Cancel { get; set; }

        public CommandExecutingEventArgs(SpreadsheetGear.Commands.Command command)
        {
            Command = command;
        }
    }
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>public event EventHandler&lt;CommandExecutingEventArgs&gt; CommandExecuting;
</code></pre>
<pre><code>public override bool Execute(Command command)
{
    var executingArgs = new CommandExecutingEventArgs(command);
    CommandExecuting?.Invoke(this, executingArgs);

    if (executingArgs.Cancel)
    {
        return true;
    }

    bool result = base.Execute(command);
    return result;
}
</code></pre>

Q: OWASP Dependency Check suppress swagger-ui-5.32.0.jar: swagger-ui-bundle.js and swagger-ui-es-bundle.js with dependency-check-suppressions.xml A: <p>This one had me puzzled as well. The issue is that in this case the vulnerabilityName is the full description containing newline characters etc... So the vulnerabilityName needs to incorporate this.<br />
I fixed the issue using:</p>
<pre><code>        &lt;packageUrl regex=&quot;true&quot;&gt;^pkg:javascript/DOMPurify@3\.2\.6$&lt;/packageUrl&gt;
        &lt;!-- (?s) enables DOTALL so . matches newlines — the vulnerability &quot;name&quot; is
             the full multi-line description text, not a short CVE/GHSA identifier --&gt;
        &lt;vulnerabilityName regex=&quot;true&quot;&gt;(?s).*&lt;/vulnerabilityName&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>This can probably be more refined.</p>

Q: Deserializing data uploaded by microservice A to a Hazelcast IMap in microservice B A: <p>Try to use <a href="https://hazelcast.github.io/hazelcast-nodejs-client/api/5.3.0/docs/interfaces/serialization_generic_record_GenericRecord.GenericRecord.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Generic Record Api</a> from Hazelcast 5.x version</p>
<pre><code>// In Service B - read without deserializing to class
IMap&lt;String, GenericRecord&gt; map = hazelcastInstance.getMap(&quot;myMap&quot;);
GenericRecord record = map.get(key);

String field1 = record.getString(&quot;field1&quot;);
int field2 = record.getInt32(&quot;field2&quot;);
</code></pre>

Q: Group associative array data by key suffix A: <p>Try this :</p>

<pre><code>$array = array ( "level-1" =&gt; 2, "quarter-1" =&gt; 1, "year-1" =&gt; 2014, "level-2" =&gt; 2, "quarter-2" =&gt; 2, "year-2" =&gt; 2015, "level-49" =&gt; 2, "quarter-49" =&gt; 2, "year-49" =&gt; 2015, "level-58" =&gt; 1, "quarter-58" =&gt; 1, "year-58"=&gt;2016);

foreach(array_chunk($array,3,true) as $val){
    foreach($val as $k=&gt;$v){
       if(strpos($k, "level") !== false){
           $temp    = explode("-",$k);
           $id      = $temp[1];
           $level   = $v;
       }
       if(strpos($k, "quarter") !== false){
           $quarter = $v;
       }
       if(strpos($k, "year") !== false){
           $year    = $v;
       }
    }
    echo "ID ".$id." Level ".$level." Quarter ".$quarter." Year ".$year;
    echo "&lt;br&gt;";
}
</code></pre>

<p>Output :</p>

<pre><code>ID 1 Level 2 Quarter 1 Year 2014
ID 2 Level 2 Quarter 2 Year 2015
ID 49 Level 2 Quarter 2 Year 2015
ID 58 Level 1 Quarter 1 Year 2016
</code></pre>
